(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [13 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [14 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [15 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [17 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [23 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [24 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [25 1 "// or Repl."] [47 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [50 1 "// pyVersion315 is the version under REPR_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15 (queue 252): the pin 3.15.2, its Lib on sys.path."] [58 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [59 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 19 "// what w buffers (writeErr)"] [66 2 "// enc, errs: reconfigure()'s encoding and errors, \"\" the process's (stdioConfig); lineBuf its line_buffering"] [67 2 "// (queue 286: inspect's command line reconfigures sys.stdout's errors)"] [70 2 "// writeThrough: every write flushed, write_through (py-mods-1122: create_stdio's !buffered_stdio, -u or"] [71 2 "// PYTHONUNBUFFERED; libregrtest's --fast-ci adds -u when sys.stdout.write_through is false; reconfigure sets it)"] [75 1 "// stdioUnbuffered is the start's buffered_stdio negated (pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): -u (bin/pyi python's"] [76 1 "// PYI_UNBUFFERED, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is) or PYTHONUNBUFFERED (not under -E or -I)"] [91 1 "// writeErr is a failed write's or flush's OSError (py-eval-1122: with SIGPIPE ignored a closed pipe is EPIPE, a"] [92 1 "// BrokenPipeError, as CPython's BufferedWriter raises it). bufio keeps a write error for every later write and flush, so"] [93 1 "// the buffered bytes are dropped and the writer starts again on what it buffers: json.tool's handler dup2s /dev/null over"] [94 1 "// stdout and exits with EPIPE's status, which the shutdown's flush (status 120 when it fails) leaves."] [105 1 "// encoding is the stream's encoding: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [113 1 "// errors is the stream's errors handler: reconfigure()'s, else the process's."] [127 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [146 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [162 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [167 2 "// reconfigure (textio.c's _io_TextIOWrapper_reconfigure_impl; queue 286): encoding and errors (errors \"strict\" when"] [168 2 "// only the encoding is given), line_buffering (a line written flushes), write_through and newline checked; the"] [169 2 "// encoding looked up as the codec registry has it"] [283 2 "// writelines is IOBase's (iobase.c's _io__IOBase_writelines_impl): each line given to the stream's write (queue 574:"] [284 2 "// Tools/patchcheck/reindent.py without arguments writes sys.stdout's lines so, test_reindent's test_noargs)"] [308 4 "// a write error raises (queue 253: flush_std_files reports a failed flush at shutdown, status 120)"] [336 2 "// readlines(hint=-1) and iteration (py-design-1122: json.tool --json-lines reads sys.stdin.readlines()): IOBase's,"] [337 2 "// readline until the end, a positive hint stopping once the lines read hold that many characters"] [377 2 "// close (queue 249: multiprocessing's _close_stdin closes sys.stdin in a spawned child): the standard streams are"] [378 2 "// made with closefd=False (create_stdio), so the stream is flushed and marked closed, its descriptor left open"] [386 4 "// a failed flush raises after the close (TextIOWrapper.close: flush, then the buffer's close in a finally)"] [404 1 "// The standard streams' buffer (PY6e's REQUEST: subprocess's children write sys.stdout.buffer): a binary"] [405 1 "// view of the same bufio reader or writer, so text and bytes keep their order."] [496 3 "// iteration: the native BufferedReader's slots read the port's value, which a standard stream's buffer has"] [497 3 "// not (queue 545: its readline's lines)"] [521 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [542 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [562 2 "// py-os-1124: bin/pyi python's PYI_ARGV, sys.argv's bytes as the command line gave them (\\x1f between them; read once"] [563 2 "// and removed from the environment), decoded as Py_DecodeLocale does under UTF-8 (surrogateescape): the host's"] [564 2 "// strings of configArgv lost an undecodable byte (test_cmd_line's test_invalid_utf8_arg)"] [581 31 "// a PYTHONPATH entry's undecodable bytes surrogate-escaped (py-os-1124)"] [594 2 "// the runtime's own text streams until the start replaces them (initSysStreams, queue 551): sys is made before"] [595 2 "// importlib stands, and a TextIOWrapper's codec lookup imports the encodings package"] [604 41 "// queue 553: create_stdio's None for a closed descriptor"] [613 15 "// 3.15 (queue 252, PY315-SURVEY P7): the version the standard library (3.15.2's Lib) moves with"] [620 25 "// types.SimpleNamespace (PY6b: FrozenImporter makes them)"] [622 45 "// pyi's own .pyc files (PY6b): __pycache__/NAME.arbace-314.pyc, its own magic number"] [628 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): the struct sequence of sysmodule.c's flags_desc"] [641 2 "// py-os-1124: -O, -v, -d, -B and their variables (config's optimization_level, verbose, parser_debug, write_bytecode),"] [642 2 "// and hash_randomization as config's use_hash_seed == 0 || hash_seed != 0 (PYTHONHASHSEED=0 without -R: 0)"] [654 47 "// -X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS (py-eval-1122)"] [657 2 "// -q, -E and -I (queue 296): config's quiet, use_environment and isolated (-I also -E's)"] [667 2 "// -i (queue 289): inspect and interactive; PYTHONINSPECT at start: inspect"] [674 2 "// -X utf8[=0|1] and PYTHONUTF8 (py-mods-1122: 3.14's too, pyi's default 1 kept; test_io's test_text_encoding runs"] [675 2 "// children with -X utf8=0 and -X utf8=1); -X warn_default_encoding and PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING (config's"] [676 2 "// warn_default_encoding, PEP 597: _pyio's text_encoding warns; test_io's test_check_encoding_warning)"] [686 3 "// 3.15's lazy imports (queue 239): sys.flags.lazy_imports, sys.lazy_modules and the mode's and filter's API"] [699 18 "// -X options (queue 220: bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS)"] [708 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, with CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [721 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): its call-family events (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [725 43 "// PY6c"] [728 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [729 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [735 2 "// config's pycache_prefix (py-os-1124, test_cmd_line's test_set_pycache_prefix): -X pycache_prefix=PATH, else"] [736 2 "// PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX (not under -E or -I); -X pycache_prefix with no or an empty PATH none"] [760 3 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_SystemExit, status): a tuple's items are the exception's arguments, None none"] [816 5 "// PyErr_GetExcInfo: the type, the exception, its __traceback__ (queue 223)"] [845 40 "// -1: -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [886 53 "// sys__getframe_impl's audit (queue 536)"] [892 2 "// breakpointhook (queue 304): sys_breakpointhook, $PYTHONBREAKPOINT's callable (pdb.set_trace when unset or empty, a"] [893 2 "// no-op for \"0\", a name without a dot builtins'), an unimportable one warned of and ignored; -E and -I ignore the"] [894 2 "// environment (Py_GETENV)"] [918 3 "// PyImport_Import: the leaf module (a non-empty fromlist)"] [936 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [942 4 "// _PyErr_Display: the traceback given put on an exception that has none (issue #18776)"] [950 4 "// traceback's display raises for a non-exception; the C fallback's print_exception line (queue 223)"] [959 2 "// is_remote_debug_enabled (queue 223): False, as a CPython built without Py_REMOTE_DEBUG answers (pyi has no"] [960 2 "// remote debugging, :remote-debugging); test_sys imports it at its top"] [1021 3 "// dataclasses' slots=True (gh-135228): __dict__ and __weakref__ taken out of a heap type's dict"] [1039 2 "// get_asyncgen_hooks and set_asyncgen_hooks (sysmodule.c; asyncio's event loops set theirs around run_forever):"] [1040 2 "// the running thread's hooks, a sys.asyncgen_hooks; an argument left out keeps its hook, None clears it"] [1074 2 "// _PySys_SetIntMaxStrDigits: 0 (no limit) or at least 640, sys.flags.int_max_str_digits with it (queue 202: a no-op,"] [1075 2 "// so test_decimal's PyCoverage, which sets 7000, met the 4300 digits' limit)"] [1098 2 "// sys.getprofile and sys.setprofile: the legacy profiler over sys.monitoring (queue 220, monitoring.go)"] [1105 2 "// sys.gettrace and sys.settrace: the legacy tracer over sys.monitoring (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [1132 2 "// threading.settrace_all_threads and setprofile_all_threads: every thread's trace or profile function"] [1175 24 "// its functions' __module__ \"sys\" (PY6f's REQUEST 8, as importBuiltin tags the others)"] [1179 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [1180 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [1209 1 "// displayUnencodable is sys_displayhook_unenc